  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "The top-4 experiments all use scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, and scgpt performed poorly (0.520), but pca_n2000 has never been tested in the multimodal setting. Config_045 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable comparison against the current best (config_007, 0.725 acc) — only the RNA encoder changes. This directly tests whether the RNA representation is the critical differentiator or whether the architecture (transformer aggregation + weighted fusion + ViT-L image) carries most of the signal. If pca_n2000 approaches 0.72, it confirms the architecture is the key driver and opens up many more viable configurations for the remaining 3 experiments. If it falls well short, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and we should exploit scVI variants (e.g., resnet50+concat, avgpool+weighted) in the final experiments. With 3 experiments left, resolving this uncertainty about the most important design axis is the highest-value use of the next slot."
}

